# Quick Bite design system

Use these consistently for new screens, CTAs, and marketing UI. Prefer **Tailwind utilities** that match existing components (`DashboardNavCards`, `AuthSlider`, dashboard layout).

## Brand accent (primary actions, selection, focus rings)

- **Brand green:** `#6DBE45` — primary buttons, icon tiles, text selection: `selection:bg-[#6DBE45] selection:text-white`
- **Green hover / borders:** `hover:border-[#6DBE45]/35`, `hover:bg-[#6DBE45]/5`, `focus-visible:ring-[#6DBE45]/30`, `ring-[#6DBE45]/20` (see sidebar nav)
- **Green solid blocks:** `bg-[#6DBE45]` with white/inverted icons (`brightness-0 invert`) on small icon wrappers

Do **not** introduce a second primary hue (no random blues/greens) for main CTAs unless the user asks for a redesign.

## Neutrals (surfaces and type)

- **Page background (app shell):** `bg-slate-50` for full-height layouts (dashboard)
- **Cards / panels:** `bg-white`, `border-slate-100` or `border-slate-200`, `shadow-sm` or `shadow-md`, `rounded-xl` / `rounded-2xl`
- **Primary text:** `text-slate-900`, `text-slate-800`
- **Secondary text:** `text-slate-500`, `text-slate-600`
- **Chrome / subtle borders:** `border-slate-200`, `ring-slate-100`

## Semantic tokens (shadcn)

When using `Button`, `Card`, etc., default `primary`/`secondary` map to CSS variables in `globals.css`. For **brand-colored** primary CTAs on standalone pages, use explicit `bg-[#6DBE45]` classes to match `AuthSlider` and dashboard (not only `bg-primary`).

## Patterns to reuse

- Dashboard shell: `min-h-screen bg-slate-50` + `selection:bg-[#6DBE45] selection:text-white`
- Auth-style full page: `min-h-screen bg-gray-100` (existing login/signup) **or** slate-50 to align with dashboard — stay consistent within one flow
